{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function getHeldKeys(): SvelteHeldKeys;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/svelte-hotkeys/src/getHeldKeys.svelte.ts#L38","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/svelte-hotkeys/src/getHeldKeys.svelte.ts:38"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Svelte function that returns reactive access to currently held keyboard keys."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This function uses the global KeyStateTracker and updates whenever keys are pressed\nor released."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/SvelteHeldKeys.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SvelteHeldKeys"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Object with a reactive "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"keys"},{"type":"text","value":" property"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script>\n  import { getHeldKeys } from '@tanstack/svelte-hotkeys'\n\n  const heldKeys = getHeldKeys()\n</script>\n<div>\n  Currently pressed: {heldKeys.keys.join(' + ') || 'None'}\n</div>","lang":"svelte"}],"headings":[{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction getHeldKeys(): SvelteHeldKeys;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/svelte-hotkeys/src/getHeldKeys.svelte.ts:38](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/svelte-hotkeys/src/getHeldKeys.svelte.ts#L38)\n\nSvelte function that returns reactive access to currently held keyboard keys.\n\nThis function uses the global KeyStateTracker and updates whenever keys are pressed\nor released.\n\n## Returns\n\n[`SvelteHeldKeys`](../interfaces/SvelteHeldKeys.md)\n\nObject with a reactive `keys` property\n\n## Example\n\n```svelte\n<script>\n  import { getHeldKeys } from '@tanstack/svelte-hotkeys'\n\n  const heldKeys = getHeldKeys()\n</script>\n<div>\n  Currently pressed: {heldKeys.keys.join(' + ') || 'None'}\n</div>\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: getHeldKeys\ntitle: getHeldKeys\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction getHeldKeys(): SvelteHeldKeys;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/svelte-hotkeys/src/getHeldKeys.svelte.ts:38](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/svelte-hotkeys/src/getHeldKeys.svelte.ts#L38)\n\nSvelte function that returns reactive access to currently held keyboard keys.\n\nThis function uses the global KeyStateTracker and updates whenever keys are pressed\nor released.\n\n## Returns\n\n[`SvelteHeldKeys`](../interfaces/SvelteHeldKeys.md)\n\nObject with a reactive `keys` property\n\n## Example\n\n```svelte\n<script>\n  import { getHeldKeys } from '@tanstack/svelte-hotkeys'\n\n  const heldKeys = getHeldKeys()\n</script>\n<div>\n  Currently pressed: {heldKeys.keys.join(' + ') || 'None'}\n</div>\n```\n"}
